 kit workspace - shows a workspace's git: its remotes, branches, worktrees, commits, and tags

   one of
   *kit workspace*  shows a workspace's git: its remotes, branches, worktrees, commits, and tags

     --text   --json   --jq
                           prints the picture as text, even on a terminal

   --stages       prints the stages the picture draws, one per line, in order, the same over any
                  workspace
   --marks        prints a mark per stage, as one JSON object, which changes when what the stage
                  draws does
   repos          each member of the workspace, cloned or not: its forge, its clone, its desk's
                  branch, its worktrees, and the local branches no checkout has
   remotes        each remote: its forge, its organization and repository, its URL, its default
                  branch, and its branches, counted
   branches       each branch: a remote's, with the local branches that pull from it, and each local
                  branch whose upstream is gone or that has none, with its commit and the worktree
                  it is checked out in
   worktrees      each worktree, the desk first: its branch, what it is ahead and behind its
                  upstream and the default branch, and its paths changed and untracked
   commits        the commits the local branches hold and the default branch does not, the newest
                  first: each one's branches, whether a remote has it, and the issue its subject
                  starts with
   tags           the tags, the newest first: annotated or lightweight, their commit, and their
                  tagger


 kit workspace
